 {
  "coord": "274:6",
  "verdict": "FAIL",
  "category": "omission",
  "note": "Source says the two glanced vainly at the onlookers; \"vainly\" was dropped.",
  "replacement": "Twelve sharpshooters with muskets stepped out of the ranks with a firm, even tread and halted eight paces from the post. Pierre turned away so as not to see what was about to happen. Suddenly there was a crackling, rolling roar that seemed to him louder than the most terrible thunder, and he looked around. There was some smoke, and the Frenchmen, pale and with trembling hands, were busy near the pit. Two more prisoners were brought forward. These two looked around vainly at the onlookers in the same way, with the same look, silently begging for protection. They plainly could not understand or believe what was going to happen to them. They could not believe it because they alone knew what their lives meant to them, and so they neither understood nor believed that anyone could take them away."
 },
